= Maria Spiridonova

Spiridonova (1884-1941), who shot a governor in 1906 and was tortured for it, is the leader of the Left SRs and the heroine of the villages. She drew the peasant congresses to the left.

- @action
- @root: Return to main

@action
title: Peasant Congress
subtitle: Spiridonova turns the peasants' deputies to the left.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer > 0 : [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next advisor action. ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.advisor_action_timer = 6;
Q.last_advisor_action = 1;
Q.month_actions += 1;
RO.boost(Q, {peasants: 8, soldiers: 2}); Q.peasant_organised = (Q.peasant_organised || 0) + 1; RO.add(Q, {rel_ally: -3}); RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 1, -1);
!}

Spiridonova spoke at the provincial peasant congresses, and the delegates followed her. The SR leaders say that she hypnotises them.

